+## Measured: 09 on the tablet (2026-09-13)
+
+[Raw runs and experimental patches](../runs/rung09-q8-20260913/).
+
+The ARMv7 compiler was calling `dot_q8_block()` for every 32 values. Adding
+`[[gnu::always_inline]] inline` removes that call and the transfer of its integer
+result through a CPU register. Arithmetic and addition order stay unchanged.
+
+| Build | Decode tok/s ± sample std | TTFT ± sample std |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Baseline, rung 08 | 6.278 ± 0.016 | 2.535 ± 0.069 s |
+| **Inline helper (retained)** | **6.490 ± 0.081** | 2.539 ± 0.033 s |
+| Vector accumulation (experiment only) | 6.443 ± 0.030 | 2.272 ± 0.008 s |
+
+Inlining improves decode **3.4%** in this short comparison. Two runs per build,
+after one warmup each: baseline, inline, vector, vector, inline, baseline.
+SmolLM2-135M Q8, batch 8, two threads, context 512, the 26-token lighthouse
+prompt, greedy seed 1, 64 generated tokens. UI active, `ondemand` governor.
+
+Vector accumulation reduces FP32 lanes once per row instead of reducing integer
+lanes per block. It cuts TTFT by **10.4%**, but changes rounding: host logits
+differ by up to 1.09 at eight tested positions. All six tablet texts match;
+that is not an accuracy evaluation. The patch is saved, but not retained.
+
+The inline build matches baseline host logits exactly at those positions.
+Host tests, ASan/UBSan, formatting, and tablet Q8 kernel tests pass.
+
